<title>SOUTH AFRICA: Fransaf sees heavy trade in bookover deals.</title>
<headline>Fransaf sees heavy trade in bookover deals.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1997-06-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>South African plastics manufacturer Fransaf Ltd had its trading volumes boosted on Monday by three bookover deals, dealers said.</p>
<p>The deals, all done by Hysamer Stals, saw 3.35 million shares change hands as the broker lined up both buyers and sellers of the stock.</p>
<p>The shares was unmoved at 180 cents, but volumes of 3.366 million shares traded made the stock the busiest by volume on the Johannesburg Stock Exchange by 0935 GMT.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482 1003</p>
